{
  "id": "semantic_tokens/preprocessor/08_empty_macros",
  "topic": "semantic_tokens",
  "subtopic": "preprocessor",
  "title": "Empty and control-flow macros",
  "summary": "A macro that expands to nothing is `empty`, one that can leave the function `controlFlow`",
  "prose": "Both modifiers mark the macro's name at its definition and at every\nexpansion. The arguments an empty macro drops never reach the compiler\nand are `inactive`, like the code of an untaken branch.",
  "status": "supported",
